# Testing

## Naming Convention

- Unit test method names MUST follow:
  `[methodName]_[stateUnderTest]_[expectedBehavior]`
- Example: `mapCellInfoNr_withValidPci_returnsCorrectDomainModel`.

## Mapper Coverage

- Every mapper that converts a raw Android framework class (`CellInfoLte`,
  `CellInfoNr`, `PhysicalChannelConfig`, etc.) into an internal domain model
  MUST have isolated unit tests. This is not optional.
- Tests must construct/mock the framework input directly — never depend on
  a real device or emulator radio state.

## Testing Stack

- JUnit5 (Jupiter) for test execution, run via the `de.mannodermaus.android-junit5`
  Gradle plugin, **pinned to `1.10.2.0`**. This is a deliberate downgrade from
  the plugin's current `de.mannodermaus.android-junit` / `android-junit-framework`
  line (2.0.0+): every release from 2.0.0 onward bundles an instrumentation
  artifact (`android-test-core`) requiring Kotlin 2.1+ (2.3 by 2.0.1), which is
  incompatible with this project's pinned Kotlin 1.9.24 toolchain (see
  tech-stack.mdc). Plugin `1.10.2.0` is the last release whose bundled
  instrumentation artifacts (`1.5.0`) were built against Kotlin 1.9.23.
- Do not bump this plugin past the `1.x` (`android-junit5`) line — and do not
  rename it back to `de.mannodermaus.android-junit` — until the project's
  Kotlin version is deliberately raised to 2.1+ as well. JUnit 6 support does
  not exist in this plugin line at all (it was introduced alongside the
  Kotlin 2.1+ jump in 2.0.0), so this project stays on JUnit 5 (Jupiter) by
  necessity, not just by minSdk policy.
- MockK for mocking framework dependencies (`CellInfo` subtypes,
  `TelephonyManager`, `PhysicalChannelConfig`, etc.).
- Turbine for testing Flow emissions (not `kotlinx-coroutines-test`).

## Modem Edge Cases

- Tests must cover modem edge cases, including sentinel/unavailable values
  such as `Int.MAX_VALUE` returned for a radio parameter (e.g. RSRP,
  EARFCN) when the value is unavailable — assert these map to `null` (or the
  documented "unknown" representation), not the raw sentinel.
